<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Paurava kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">350 BCE – 317 BCE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Punjab kingdom of Porus, who fought Alexander the Great at the Battle of the Hydaspes in 326 BCE and kept his throne as an ally.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Paurava kingdom lay between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jhelum">Jhelum</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chenab">Chenab</a> rivers in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, in modern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/islamic-republic-of-pakistan">Pakistan</a>, and emerged after Achaemenid control of the region faded in the 4th century BCE. Its king, called <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porus">Porus</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a>, perhaps from the Vedic clan name <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/purus">Puru</a>, was a rival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambhi">Ambhi</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-taxila">Kingdom of Taxila</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Greek historians describe a strong monarchy with an army of infantry, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariots</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-elephant">war elephants</a>. At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-hydaspes">Battle of the Hydaspes</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jhelum">Jhelum</a>, in 326 BCE, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porus">Porus</a> faced Alexander with his elephants; Alexander crossed the river by surprise and won. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arrian">Arrian</a> reports that the wounded Porus, asked how he wished to be treated, answered: like a king. Little else is known of the kingdom's society.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Alexander restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porus">Porus</a> and enlarged his territory as far as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beas">Beas</a>. After Alexander's death Porus was murdered around 317 BCE by the Macedonian officer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eudemus-general">Eudemus</a>, and his lands passed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a>. The meeting of Porus and Alexander became a celebrated story in both Greek and Indian memory.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 350 BCE – 317 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:52.74%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>350 BCE – 317 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Porus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Vedic religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Prakrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Porus, Pauravas</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-334&amp;focus=paurava-kingdom" aria-label="Paurava kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6472 1113 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Paurava kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5548 987h0M7253 1492h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6792 1369h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M6792 1369h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Pakistan. <a href="/atlas?year=-334&amp;focus=paurava-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

